# Architecture

Flutter app lives in `app/`. Follow this on every change. When you touch a messy file, **split toward this layout** — do not grow god files (`tracker_repository.dart` is the one left).

## Features (`app/lib/features/<name>/`)

- `data/` — repository, local queries, feature DTOs
- `services/` — pure domain logic (no Flutter, no I/O)
- `presentation/controllers/` — Riverpod notifiers
- `presentation/providers/` — Riverpod providers
- `presentation/screens/` — one screen per file
- `presentation/widgets/` — feature-only UI

## Shared

- Model used by **more than one feature** → `app/lib/core/domain/models/`. Never import a model from `features/A` into `features/B`.
- `app/lib/core/services/` is **infrastructure only** (sync, connectivity, env). No scoring/stats/XP-style business logic.
- `app/lib/core/theme/` — tokens and ThemeData only (`app_palette.dart`, `app_typography.dart`, `app_theme.dart`). No feature widgets.
- Generic chrome → `app/lib/core/widgets/`. Feature-specific chrome stays in the feature.

## Placement test

- Phone/system? → core. User’s team/game/stats? → feature.
- UI used in one feature? → that feature’s `widgets/`. App-wide? → core widgets or theme.

## State

Riverpod. Routing: go_router. Local DB: Drift. Remote: Supabase. Scoring engine, game replay and stats aggregator stay **pure functions** with unit tests.
